/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  pairLookup01_catalogue_ladder
  =============================

  WHAT IT IS.  The student's FIRST question about a binary -- "what does
  Choupo have for this pair?" -- asked as ONE operation that answers in a
  fixed byte budget (2048 bytes of card text, held by check_lookup_budget)
  with an EVIDENCE CARD, never a number invented to fill a gap.  The four
  operations walk the honesty ladder (DEV.md 4c C227, slice a):

      p_curated    ethanol + water       a catalogue pair record: the
                                         paste-ready source entry, validity,
                                         provenance
      p_regressed  acetone + ethanol     Choupo's own regression (fittedInCase,
                                         interim) with its held-out verdict
      p_estimate   acetone + cyclo-      no pair record, both carry UNIFAC
                   hexane                groups: SAID to be an estimate, with
                                         the measured warning (DEV.md C219)
      p_none       1Pentadecanol +       a component only in the group-
                   water                 estimate lake: "I do not have this
                                         pair"

  HOW IT READS.  The operations read the INSTALLATION catalogue (a question
  about the catalogue), never the case's own constant/.  The card carries what
  the records carry today; what the C16 chain will add (laboratories, archive
  sha256, extraction filter, fit AAD) is listed under announcedAbsent and
  never filled.  The rung "servable from the measurement archive but not yet
  fitted" is slice (b) and the card says it does not exist yet.  Pinned: the
  TIER WORD of each card and its byte count; the numbers a card quotes live in
  the records, which have their own gates.  The thermoPhysPropDict is a
  placeholder the bench requires; no op reads it.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
operations
(
    { name p_curated;   type pairLookup;  components ( ethanol water ); }
    { name p_regressed; type pairLookup;  components ( acetone ethanol ); }
    { name p_estimate;  type pairLookup;  components ( acetone cyclohexane ); }
    { name p_none;      type pairLookup;  components ( 1Pentadecanol water ); }
);
